A well-blinded RCT is considered the [ gold standard
](/wiki/Gold_standard_\(test\) "Gold standard \(test\)") for clinical trials.
Blinded RCTs are commonly used to test the [ efficacy
](/wiki/Efficacy#Medicine "Efficacy") of medical [ interventions
](/wiki/Health_intervention "Health intervention") and may additionally
provide information about adverse effects, such as [ drug reactions
](/wiki/Adverse_drug_reactions "Adverse drug reactions") . A randomized
controlled trial can provide compelling evidence that the study treatment
causes an effect on human health.  [6]

